  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.1.1-beta\n\t\t\t- Aligns Threading with the established 1.3.1 dependency and restores the existing green test baseline.\n\t\t\t- Adds the opt-in IPathPlaceable contract in the Placement namespace for existing record types.\n\t\t\t- Preserves existing implementation and frozen contract snapshots.\n\t\t\t2.1.x\n\t\t\t- To standardize case and improve refactorability, many signatures accept user-defined enum types in place of strings. We refer to this pattern as StdEnum, and this release expands the signatures that support it.\n\t\t\t- OnPropertyChanged([CallerMemberName]) now laterals to a proper (sender, e) signature.\n\t\t\t- DualKeyLookup is now observable.\n\t\t\t- DualKeyLookup now respects @throw on the setter when overwriting an existing mapping with a different value.\n\t\t\t- Added DualKeyLookup.BeforeModifyMapping for intercepting or canceling overwrites.\n\n\t\t\t2.0.x\n\t\t\t- Added Placer extensions for path-based XML element placement.\n\t\t\t- Enhanced enum support with safety asserts for non-nullable named enum types in edge cases.\n\t\t\t- Added a [Placement] attribute for Enum so individual enum types can declare storage as either XElement or XBoundAttribute.\n\t\t\t- Try methods are now idiomatic. Any bool @throw = false arguments have been removed from their signatures.\n\t\t\t- Trailing path delimiters on fqpath (Placer and Place) are now removed.\n\t\t\t- Unit testing in this release is broader and more informative; the repos document both test coverage and working usage insights.\n\t\t\t- Minor 2.0.x improvements include enum key exposure and enhanced XML placement APIs.",
